# These files are consumed byte-for-byte, not read as prose.
#
# The generated skill bundles copies of the SVGs and of brand.json, and CI asserts
# the copies are identical to the originals. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) git rewrites every LF on checkout, and any consumer that checksums these
# files sees a different digest on Windows than on Linux CI. The Plainsight Brain
# does exactly that: content/brand/brand-kit.sync.json records a sha256 per file.
#
# So never translate them.
*.svg    -text
*.json   -text
*.css    -text
*.js     -text
*.potx   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary

# The generated skill is byte-compared against a fresh generation, and the
# generator writes LF. Without this, `generate_skill.py --check` reports the file
# as stale on every Windows clone while passing on Linux CI: a guard that cries
# wolf is a guard people learn to ignore. It also means the SKILL.md a colleague
# installs is identical on every platform.
skill/plainsight-brand/SKILL.md  -text
